olor:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Tennessee Eviction Notice Rules: Notice Types, Days and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Tennessee</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Tennessee Eviction Notice Rules: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Tennessee Eviction Notice Rules sale</li><li>Turn the Tennessee Eviction Notice Rules offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Tennessee House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Tennessee law requires a landlord to give a specific written notice before filing an eviction, and the number of days depends on the reason.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>URLTA notice periods listed: fourteen-day, seven-day (repeat violations), three-day (violence, threats, unsanitary conditions); waiver of notice for nonpayment is possible. (TN Courts, Landlord Tenant Update presentation; <a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/landlordtenant_-_presentation_0.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Non-URLTA notices listed: 14 day, 30 day, 3 day. (TN Courts, Landlord Tenant Update presentation; <a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/landlordtenant_-_presentation_0.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>When judgment is for the plaintiff and a writ of possession is awarded, it is executed and the plaintiff restored to possession immediately. (Tenn. Code Ann. 29-18 (writ of possession), per TN Courts presentation; <a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/landlordtenant_-_presentation_0.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Service: personal service on an adult in possession, or after three attempts on different dates, posting plus mailing at least six days before the hearing. (Tenn. Code Ann. 29-18-115 (shown as 29-18-15 in slide), per TN Courts presentation; <a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/landlordtenant_-_presentation_0.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Continuance maximum 15 days unless parties agree, landlord consents or no court is held; defendant appeal within 10 days (29-18-129); certiorari to circuit court within 30 days. (Tenn. Code Ann. 29-18-118, 29-18-129, per TN Courts presentation; <a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/landlordtenant_-_presentation_0.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Tennessee?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Tennessee houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Tennessee Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Tennessee Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-probate-laws/'>Tennessee Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Tennessee guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-tennessee/'>We buy houses in Tennessee</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/landlordtenant_-_presentation_0.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>TN Courts, Landlord Tenant Update presentation</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Tennessee Eviction Notice Rules, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Tennessee\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-tennessee/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Tennessee Eviction Notice: Types and Days\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-eviction-notice/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Tennessee Eviction Notice: Types and Days", "rank_math_description": "Tennessee eviction notice rules: notice types, required days, which court hears the case and selling a rental. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "tennessee eviction notice"}, {"slug": "tennessee-probate-laws", "title": "Tennessee Probate Laws: Who Inherits, Small Estates and Selling the House", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Tennessee Probate Laws: Who Inherits, Small Estates and Selling the House</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Tennessee</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Tennessee Probate Laws: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Tennessee Probate Laws sale</li><li>Turn the Tennessee Probate Laws offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Tennessee House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>Tennessee probate law decides who inherits when there is no will, when a small estate can skip full probate, and who can sign a deed for an inherited house.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>A Small Estate (Small Estates Act, T.C.A. 30-4-101 to 30-4-105) means personal property not exceeding $50,000; it cannot transfer title to real estate. (Hawkins County Chancery Court, Small Estates Act Affidavit instructions; <a href='https://www.hawkinscountytn.gov/pdfs/small_estates_affidavit.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A small estate cannot be opened until 45 days from date of death; affidavit filed with court with death certificate; original will, if any, deposited with clerk. (Hawkins County Chancery Court, Small Estates Act Affidavit instructions; <a href='https://www.hawkinscountytn.gov/pdfs/small_estates_affidavit.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Intestate spouse share: if there are surviving issue, either one-third or a child&#x27;s share (search/guide excerpt); any part of an estate not disposed of by will passes to heirs in the same manner. (Tennessee Probate Guide (TN Courts), general rules of descent; <a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/probate_manual_final.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>If there is no surviving issue or parent, the estate goes to brothers and sisters and their issue by representation. (Tennessee Probate Guide (TN Courts); <a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/probate_manual_final.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Tennessee?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Tennessee houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Tennessee Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Tennessee Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-eviction-notice/'>Tennessee Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Tennessee guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-tennessee/'>We buy houses in Tennessee</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://www.hawkinscountytn.gov/pdfs/small_estates_affidavit.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Hawkins County Chancery Court, Small Estates Act Affidavit instruction</a></li><li><a href='https://www.tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/probate_manual_final.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>Tennessee Probate Guide (TN Courts), general rules of descent</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Tennessee Probate Laws, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Tennessee\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-tennessee/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Tennessee Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-probate-laws/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Tennessee Probate Laws: Inheritance and Sales", "rank_math_description": "Tennessee probate laws: who inherits without a will, small estate rules, deadlines and selling an inherited house. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "tennessee probate laws"}, {"slug": "tennessee-tax-deed-and-tax-lien-sales", "title": "Tennessee Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: Process, Redemption and Selling First", "content": "<!-- wp:html -->\n<style>.wsp-hero{position:relative;margin:0 calc(-50vw + 50%);padding:5rem 1.5rem;background-image:none;background:linear-gradient(170deg,#12293f 0%,#0c1c2e 46%,#060c16 100%);overflow:hidden;}.wsp-hero-inner{max-width:1216px;margin:0 auto;display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.1fr 1fr;gap:2.5rem;align-items:center;}.wsp-hero-left{text-align:center;}.wsp-hero-left h1{color:#fff;font-size:2.6rem;font-weight:800;line-height:1.15;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left h2{color:#fff;font-weight:300;font-size:1.3rem;margin:0 0 1rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-hero-left p{color:#fff;font-size:1rem;font-weight:300;max-width:500px;margin:0 auto 1.5rem;text-shadow:1px 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3);}.wsp-btn-outline{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;border:2px solid #fff;border-radius:30px;padding:.6rem 1.4rem;font-weight:600;color:#fff;text-decoration:none;font-size:.95rem;}.wsp-btn-outline:hover{background:#fff;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-hero-right iframe{width:100%;min-height:560px;border:none;border-radius:4px;}.wsp-wrap{max-width:900px;margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 1.5rem 4rem;}@media (max-width:900px){.wsp-hero-inner{grid-template-columns:1fr;}.wsp-hero-left h1{font-size:2.1rem;}}.wsp-wrap h3{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:4px solid #3182CE;border-radius:8px;padding:.9rem 1.25rem;margin:1.75rem 0 0;font-size:1.05rem;font-weight:700;color:#1A202C;}.wsp-wrap h3+p{background:#fff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-top:none;border-radius:0 0 8px 8px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin:0 0 .25rem;color:#444;}.wsp-wrap table td{vertical-align:top;}.chb-cta p{margin:0}.wsp-related{margin:2.5rem 0 1rem}.wsp-related h2{font-size:1.3rem;margin-bottom:1rem;font-weight:600;}.wsp-related-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(220px,1fr));gap:1rem;}.wsp-related-card{background:#f8fafc;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-radius:8px;padding:1.1rem 1.25rem;}.wsp-related-card a{font-weight:700;color:var(--global-palette1, #3182CE);text-decoration:none;}.wsp-related-card a:hover{text-decoration:underline;}.wsp-related-card p{margin:.35rem 0 0;font-size:.9rem;color:#555;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call{background:#E0A83C !important;border:2px solid #E0A83C !important;color:#16203A !important;font-size:1.25rem !important;font-weight:800 !important;padding:1rem 2.2rem !important;border-radius:40px !important;box-shadow:0 0 0 4px rgba(224,168,60,.25),0 8px 26px rgba(224,168,60,.5) !important;text-shadow:none !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call strong{color:#16203A !important;}.wsp-hero a.wsp-btn-call:hover{background:#fff !important;border-color:#fff !important;}</style><div class='wsp-hero'><div class='wsp-hero-inner'><div class='wsp-hero-left'><h1>Tennessee Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: Process, Redemption and Selling First</h1><div class=wsp-kicker>Cash Home Buyers in Tennessee</div><div class=wsp-speed><span>Cash Offer in 24 Hours</span></div><ul class=wsp-checks><li>Tennessee Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales: inherited, behind on payments, tenants or repairs, we buy the house as-is</li><li>No fees, commissions or closing costs on a Tennessee Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales sale</li><li>Turn the Tennessee Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales offer down and you owe us nothing</li></ul><h2>Selling a Tennessee House? Get a Cash Offer</h2><p>We buy as-is.</p><p><a class='wsp-btn-outline wsp-btn-call' href='tel:424-435-2326'>Call or Text <strong>&nbsp;(424) 435-2326</strong></a></p></div><div class='wsp-hero-right'><iframe src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/widget/form/zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' data-form-id='zKzKbSeB3aqwWwE8NNxO' title='Cash Offer Form'></iframe><br /><script src='https://connect.cashhomebuyersca.com/js/form_embed.js' async></script></div></div></div><div class='wsp-wrap'><p><em>Last updated November 14, 2026.</em></p><p><strong>When property tax goes unpaid in Tennessee, the statutes allow the taxing authority to sell a lien or the property itself, and they give the owner a set time to redeem.</strong></p><h2>What the official sources say</h2><ul><li>Redemption: one year from entry of the order confirming the tax sale to the tax sale purchaser. (T.C.A. 67-5-2701(a)(1)(D), per TN Courts delinquent tax handout; <a href='https://tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/Chancellors%20Luncheon%20-%20Delinquent%20Taxes%20-%20Handout.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Redemption period can be shortened to 30 days if the purchaser shows the property is vacant and abandoned by 3 periodic inspections over two months at different times of day. (T.C.A. 67-5-2701(n), per TN Courts delinquent tax handout; <a href='https://tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/Chancellors%20Luncheon%20-%20Delinquent%20Taxes%20-%20Handout.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>A redeeming taxpayer pays delinquent taxes, penalty, interest, court costs and interest on the purchase price at 1% per month, levied from the date of sale and on the first day of each month until 30 days after the motion to redeem is filed. (T.C.A. 67-5-2701(b); Tenn. Attorney General Opinion 15-22; <a href='https://www.tn.gov/content/dam/tn/attorneygeneral/documents/ops/2015/op15-22.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li><li>Motion for lawful charges must be filed within 30 days after mailing of the notice of redemption. (T.C.A. 67-5-2701(d), per TN Courts delinquent tax handout; <a href='https://tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/Chancellors%20Luncheon%20-%20Delinquent%20Taxes%20-%20Handout.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>source</a>)</li></ul><div class=\"chb-cta\" style=\"margin:32px 0;border-radius:10px;background:linear-gradient(120deg,#0F1C2E 0%,#16293F 100%);padding:28px 32px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:20px;flex-wrap:wrap;color:#fff;\"><div style=\"max-width:600px;\"><div style=\"font-size:12px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:2px;color:#E0A83C;text-transform:uppercase;margin-bottom:6px;\">Selling in Tennessee?</div><div style=\"font-weight:800;font-size:20px;line-height:1.35;color:#fff;\">We buy Tennessee houses as-is, with no commission, no repairs and no closing costs to you.</div></div><a href=\"#\" onclick=\"var f=document.querySelector('iframe[data-form-id]');if(f){f.scrollIntoView({behavior:'smooth',block:'center'});return false;}\" style=\"flex-shrink:0;padding:14px 24px;border-radius:8px;background:#E0A83C;color:#16203A;font-size:14px;font-weight:800;text-decoration:none;white-space:nowrap;\">Get My Cash Offer &rarr;</a></div><div class='wsp-related'><div class='wsp-related-grid'><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-squatters-rights-adverse-possession/'>Tennessee Squatters Rights and Adverse Possession</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-landlord-tenant-law-tenant-rights/'>Tennessee Landlord Tenant Law and Tenant Rights</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-eviction-notice/'>Tennessee Eviction Notice: Types and Days</a><p>Official sources.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-guides-by-city-and-county/'>Tennessee guides by city and county</a><p>Every local guide we publish.</p></div><div class='wsp-related-card'><a href='https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-tennessee/'>We buy houses in Tennessee</a><p>How a cash offer works.</p></div></div></div><h2>Sources</h2><ul><li><a href='https://tncourts.gov/sites/default/files/docs/Chancellors%20Luncheon%20-%20Delinquent%20Taxes%20-%20Handout.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>T.C.A. 67-5-2701(a)(1)(D), per TN Courts delinquent tax handout</a></li><li><a href='https://www.tn.gov/content/dam/tn/attorneygeneral/documents/ops/2015/op15-22.pdf' target='_blank' rel='noreferrer noopener nofollow'>T.C.A. 67-5-2701(b); Tenn. Attorney General Opinion 15-22</a></li></ul><p><em>General information for Tennessee Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales, not legal or tax advice. Confirm details with the official office or a licensed professional.</em></p><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\", \"@type\": \"BreadcrumbList\", \"itemListElement\": [{\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 1, \"name\": \"Home\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 2, \"name\": \"Tennessee\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/we-buy-houses-in-tennessee/\"}, {\"@type\": \"ListItem\", \"position\": 3, \"name\": \"Tennessee Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales\", \"item\": \"https://cashhomebuyersca.com/tennessee-tax-deed-and-tax-lien-sales/\"}]}</script></div>\n<!-- /wp:html -->", "status": "publish", "rank_math_title": "Tennessee Tax Deed and Tax Lien Sales", "rank_math_description": "Tennessee tax deed and tax lien sales: who runs the sale, interest, redemption periods and selling before the sale. Official sources.", "rank_math_focus_keyword": "tennessee tax deed sales"}]